description:
## For...of
Accessing arrays by index works, but it's clunky. `for...of` loops through every element directly:
```ts
const names: string[] = ["Alice", "Bob", "Steve"];
for (const name of names) {
    console.log(name);
}
// Alice
// Bob
// Steve
```
No index needed. Clean and simple.

